        "id": 1000107
      },
      "writtenOn": "2012-09-05T19:20:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, it\u0027s already an input.  I guess I assumed that \"gpio_set_level\" wouldn\u0027t do anything in that case.\n\n...and it doesn\u0027t appear to.  It just sets the STM32_GPIO_BSRR_OFF register, which ought to be ignored if we are still an input.\n\nMy hope was to avoid glitching the lines.  Generally when you switch from input to output you want to put a value into the set register _before_ changing direction.\n\n\nAlso note that once I turn it to an output I turn it to an \"open drain\" output.  I believe that means to let the line float high when you set its value to \"1\".",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAPn//1JY\u003d",
      "revId": "ff1c83d81d5d170dd982e4fce990594a49399c85",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
